  ("18540","Justin","2026-06-30T09:59:49.743+0900",
   "<custom data-type=\"mention\" data-id=\"id-0\">@Harry</custom> — OMH-661 (TanStack Query provider + SSR hydration) is implemented and moved to In Review: [PR #73](https://github.com/ohmyhotelco/ohmyhotel-monorepo/pull/73) (draft, base master).\n\n**Delivered:**\n\n* QueryClient provider in root — getQueryClient(): fresh per request on the server (no cross-request leak), singleton in the browser; staleTime 60s (refetch-flash guard).\n* ApiClientProvider + useApiClient context (shared-data hooks take an axios instance by DI). Anonymous client for public Phase 1 content; OMH-660 swaps in the cookie-aware one.\n* Model B (loader prefetch → dehydrate → HydrationBoundary) as the route standard. API decisions verified against current docs (Context7: TanStack Query v5.90.3, React Router v7.9.4).\n\n**Verified (Node 22):** typecheck + build green; the hydration test asserts queryFn is not re-called after hydrate (cache hit, staleTime>0) = no refetch flash. Devtools confirmed tree-shaken from the prod client bundle.\n\n**Deferred / coordination:** page-specific hooks → OMH-706+; cookie-aware request-scoped client + getLoadContext (Path β) → OMH-660; MSW/component-render tests → OMH-653. app/root.tsx overlaps OMH-659/660 → whichever merges second rebases (trivial)."),
  ("18541","Justin","2026-06-30T10:12:58.297+0900",
   "**Independent review round (codex + quality-reviewer)** — both confirmed the SSR-hydration core correct (per-request server client, no module-singleton leak, `staleTime` refetch-flash guard, single react-query instance/context). codex: FIX-FIRST; quality-reviewer: 4/5 SHIP. Fixes applied (commit `85336f5dd`, PR #73):\n\n* `resolveEnvironment()` — completed the Vite-mode → `OmhEnvironment` mapping (local/dev/staging/prod/br1 pass-through; development→dev, production→prod) and throw on unknown, instead of silently routing `--mode local`/`--mode br1` to dev (wrong API base URL). Build-time `MODE` is documented as a dev/fallback; production env-correctness is OMH-660 via the runtime-env injected client.\n* **Test forward-protection** — pinned `// @vitest-environment node` so the \"fresh client per server call\" assertion survives OMH-653's DOM harness (it would otherwise flip to the browser singleton and FAIL).\n* **devtools** — pinned `@tanstack/react-query-devtools` to 5.101.1 (== resolved react-query) to clear the dev-only peer skew; single instance preserved.\n* **Docs** — recorded the per-loader (Path α) client rule in query-client.ts.\n\nBy design, deferred + documented (not blocking): a live loader→HydrationBoundary route → OMH-706+; the runtime-env (server `process.env`) client → OMH-660; component-render + MSW tests → OMH-653.\n\nRe-verified (Node 22): typecheck + test (2/2) + build green; devtools confirmed absent from the prod client bundle."),
  ("18545","Justin","2026-06-30T10:22:54.545+0900",
   "**Review round 2 (codex + quality-reviewer)** — both verified all four round-1 fixes correct (quality-reviewer 4.5/5 SHIP; codex FIX-FIRST). They independently converged on one remaining item. Fixed (commit `a4b03fecd`, PR #73):\n\n* `resolveEnvironment()` `\"test\"` mode — Vitest sets `MODE=\"test\"`, so a future component test mounting the provider tree without an injected client would hit the unknown-mode throw. Added `case \"test\" → \"local\"`; new `api-client.test.ts` asserts `createWebPcApiClient()` does not throw under `MODE=test` (regression guard). No current break — purely forward-protection for OMH-653/706+ tests.\n* **root.tsx comment** — corrected \"pins the same version\" → web-pc uses the same react-query _range_ (`^5.62.7`) as shared-data; pnpm dedupes to a single instance.\n\nDeferred (out of web-pc scope, noted for follow-up):\n\n* Promote `@tanstack/react-query` to a **peerDependency** in `shared-data` so the single-instance invariant is structural, not dedup-dependent → **OMH-657**.\n* Root `ErrorBoundary` export (framework-mode convention; more valuable now there's a throw path) → **OMH-660** (layout/shell).\n\nRe-verified (Node 22): typecheck + test (3/3) + build green; devtools still absent from the prod client bundle. Two independent reviewers now converge ship-ready."),
  ("18550","Justin","2026-06-30T10:32:06.717+0900",
   "**Review round 3 (codex + quality-reviewer)** — quality-reviewer **5/5, ship** (\"no remaining actionable defect within OMH-661's own scope; every remaining deduction is cross-ticket or by-design\"). Score trajectory 4 → 4.5 → 5: the r2 half-point was the `MODE=test` footgun, now fixed. codex: FIX-FIRST on one item — the new `api-client.test.ts` was implicit (only asserted `not.toThrow()`, which any valid mode satisfies).\n\nFixed (commit `4020a62e1`, PR #73): strengthened the test so the `test → local` mapping is **observable** — it now asserts `import.meta.env.MODE === \"test\"` and that the default client's `baseURL` resolves to the `pc:local` config (not merely \"did not throw\"). Comment corrected too. Re-verified (Node 22): typecheck + test (3/3) + build green.\n\n**In-scope status: clean.** Both reviewers now converge — the OMH-661 web-pc code (query-client / api-client / root + tests) has no remaining defect.\n\n**Cross-ticket structural follow-ups (the only residuals, not OMH-661 defects):**\n\n* Promote `@tanstack/react-query` to a **peerDependency** in `shared-data` → makes the single-QueryClient-context invariant structural instead of pnpm-dedup-dependent → **OMH-657** (flagged by quality-reviewer as \"the structural backstop for OMH-661\").\n* Root `ErrorBoundary` export → **OMH-660** (layout/shell).\n\n"),
